course: dictionary
lesson: 10340
title: What is a transaction?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A transaction is an act of buying or selling something, or of moving money. Paying in a shop, taking out cash or sending money online are all transactions. Each one is an item on your list of money in and money out.
explain: The example says: «A transaction is a payment in or out; a statement or app lists them, like £2.50 + £4.99 + £1.20 = £8.69 spent in a week.» Three payments were made, so three transactions are added together to find the total spent.
explain: Look at the clue words: payment, statement, spent. They tell you the word is about money. Ask yourself: is money moving here? If yes, it is probably a transaction.
fact: A transaction is an act of buying or selling something, or of moving money.
fact: Paying in a shop, withdrawing cash and sending money online are all transactions.
fact: «£2.50 + £4.99 + £1.20 = £8.69» shows three transactions adding up to a total of £8.69 spent.
fact: In a formal sense, a transaction is any piece of business or exchange between people or organisations.
fact: In computing, a transaction is a set of actions that must all happen together or not at all, as in banking systems.
exercise: Which of these is a transaction? | Reading a book | Singing a song | Walking to school | *Paying for a sandwich with a card
exercise: «£2.50 + £4.99 + £1.20 = £8.69 spent in a week.» How many transactions are in this sum? | Two | Seven | *Three | One
exercise: What does a bank statement or app list? | Your pets | Your favourite songs | The weather for the week | *Your transactions, the money in and out
test: Ella makes two transactions, one for £4.25 and one for £3.75. What is the total she spent? | £8.50 | *£8.00 | £9.00 | £7.50
test: In computing, what must a transaction do? | Always take exactly one minute | *Happen all together or not at all | Be written in pencil | Happen only in a shop
exam: Which is a safe habit about transactions? | Share your bank details with anyone who asks | Keep your PIN written on your card | Send money to people you have only met online | *Check your transactions regularly and never share your bank details
